2. Social LSTM: Human Trajectory Prediction in Crowded Spaces (Alahi et al., 2016)
Method: Links multiple LSTMs with a pooling layer to predict crowded movement.
Dataset: ETH and UCY pedestrian datasets.
Advantages: Accurately models complex human movement trajectories.
Limitations: Sequential processing makes LSTMs too slow for edge processing.
Research Gap: Ultra-fast, non-sequential models for trajectory prediction.
Possible Improvements: Replaces slow LSTMs with Mamba’s parallel, linear-time architecture.
